              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Half the unit are armed with a sword and light armour and composite bow, the other half are armed with thrusting spear. One unit of Assyrian cavalry may be upgraded to Royal Guard cavalry with cavalrymen in the unit armed with both thrusting spear and composite bow and riding barded horses (+6 pts). Mounted archers in the second rank of the unit may shoot over the first rank. Assyrian armies only. (Chariot Wars p.57)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="b46d-26f1-3385-def4" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <!-- armour-save -->
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
